    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "The AIRCRAFT\nfor the\n15\nPRIVATE\nOWNER - FLYER\nPITCAIRN\nautogiro",
      "PITCAIRN\nAIRS\nViews of the complete and modern plant of Pitcairn Air-\ncraft, Inc., at Willow Grove, Pa. At the top is a bird's-eye\nview of the plant. Below at left, a glimpse of work on\nwelded steel tubing, fuselage construction.\nLower right,\nsection of rotor blade and wing construction\nThe organization responsible\nfor the Pitcairn Autogiro . .\nThe Pitcairn Autogiro is made by a company\nwith a long and successful record in the aircraft\nindustry. Beginning with the early Pitcairn\nOrowings, through the Pitcairn Mailwing air-\nmail successes, down to the present Pitcairn\nTandem-all Pitcairn products earned their\nreputation for excellence in design, material and\ncraftsmanship. The Pitcairn plant is manned\nby a personnel experienced in manufacture.\nPITCAIRN AUTOGIRO COMPANY\nPITCAIRN FIELD, WILLOW GROVE, PA.\nS. L. NO. 8\n2012\nPRINTED IN U.S. A",
      "TAKE-OFF\nWhat the prate owner\nneeds is—security\nIn nearly thirty years of existence, the airplane has not\nmade flying as commonplace as predicted. In compari-\nson with the millions who operate automobiles, only a\nfew operate airplanes, and those largely for mail and\ntransport, or military use.\nTen years ago, Juan de la Cierva foresaw a new oppor-\ntunity for growth in the field of aviation. He saw that\nThe Pitcairn Tandem, after landing on the lawn of a country\nhome, ready for take-off with a passenger\nLANDING\nmore speed per horse-power.\nGeneral specifications. Fuselage: Weight empty, 1310\nIbs.; Gross weight, 1900 Ibs.; Useful load, 590 Ibs.;\nLength of Ship, 19 ft. 5 ins.; Span of Ship, 21 ft.; Wing\narea, 57.6 sq. ft.; Ground height (clearance to rotor\nhub), 10 ft. 6½ ins. Rotor: Diameter, 40 ft.; Blade\narea, 106.5 sq. ft.; Disc area, 1260 sq. ft. Power plant:\nEngine, 160 h.p.; Gasoline capacity, 30 gals.; Oil\ncapacity, 3½ gals. Equipment: Combination pump\nand gravity fuel system with wobble pump; Dual con-\ntrols; Motor starter; Cockpit primer; Metal propeller;\nRoller-bearing semi-low-pressure wheels; Parking brakes;\nTail wheel and landing gear with Oleo shock absorbers;\nFire extinguisher; Navigation lights; Leather uphol-\nstery; Safety glass windshields front and rear cockpits;\nFull complement of necessary instruments including\ncompass; Cadmium plated fittings.\nPITCAIRN AIRCRAFT, INC.\nPITCAIRN FIELD, WILLOW GROVE, PA.\nPITCAIRN\nautogiro"
    ],
